---
// Answer-first summary for readers and AI answer engines.
---

<section class="bg-white py-16 md:py-[100px]">
  <div class="max-w-[1280px] mx-auto px-4 sm:px-8 md:px-16">
    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 lg:grid-cols-12 gap-10 lg:gap-16">
      <div class="lg:col-span-4">
        <p class="section-label mb-4">In short</p>
        <h2
          class="font-inter font-bold leading-[1.1] tracking-[-0.025em] text-sp-heading"
          style="font-size: clamp(26px, 3vw, 42px);"
        >
          What Spatia does
        </h2>
        <p class="mt-5 text-[17px] leading-[1.7] text-sp-body">
          Spatia is the intelligence layer for robots in manufacturing.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="lg:col-span-8 grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 gap-x-8 gap-y-8">
        <div>
          <h3 class="mb-2 text-[17px] font-semibold text-sp-heading">What it is</h3>
          <p class="text-[16px] leading-[1.7] text-sp-body">
            Spatia turns a part's CAD model into robot perception and station-level execution.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3 class="mb-2 text-[17px] font-semibold text-sp-heading">Who it is for</h3>
          <p class="text-[16px] leading-[1.7] text-sp-body">
            Manufacturers and system integrators deploying bin picking, vision guided robotic inspection or dynamic torque.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3 class="mb-2 text-[17px] font-semibold text-sp-heading">How it works</h3>
          <p class="text-[16px] leading-[1.7] text-sp-body">
            CAD-native perception finds the part and its 6D pose. Motion planning, gripping and SOP checks carry the job from pick to place. Built for BYOR on ROS 2, validated on UR and Flexiv.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3 class="mb-2 text-[17px] font-semibold text-sp-heading">Where to see it</h3>
          <p class="text-[16px] leading-[1.7] text-sp-body">
            At the Experience Centre in Chennai, India. Bring a part and its CAD model.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-10 flex flex-wrap gap-x-6 gap-y-3">
      <a href="/guides/picking-cell" class="text-[15px] font-semibold text-sp-green hover:underline underline-offset-4">
        How to evaluate a picking cell →
      </a>
      <a href="/glossary" class="text-[15px] font-semibold text-sp-green hover:underline underline-offset-4">
        Robotics glossary →
      </a>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
